# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository, regardless of a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, any text file first committed with LF (the default for
# most editors/tools) perpetually shows a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every git
# operation on Windows with core.autocrlf=true set - harmless, but noisy forever, and easy to
# mistake for a real uncommitted change (this is exactly what happened with
# frontend/src-tauri/Cargo.toml throughout an entire session).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries some tooling might otherwise try to text-normalize - never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.keystore binary
